  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_001 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc / 3.60 GPU hrs. RNA encoder choice shows enormous variance (scgpt drops accuracy to 0.520 vs scvi_n200 at 0.725), yet pca_n2000 — a fundamentally different linear encoder — has never been tested in the multiprofile multimodal setting. This experiment tests whether pca_n2000 can match or approach scvi_n200 while keeping all other hyperparameters at their best-known values (transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, imagenet_vit_l). Resolving the RNA encoder question is the highest-priority uncertainty: if pca_n2000 is competitive, it may offer a cheaper path; if it underperforms significantly, we confirm scvi_n200 is essential and can focus remaining budget on image-encoder variations (resnet50). Expected relative cost: pca_n2000 is a linear projection rather than a learned VAE, so training should be slightly cheaper than config_001, estimated around 2.5–3.5 GPU hours."
}

